stem="A 62-year-old man is scheduled for elective surgical aortic valve replacement next week. Preoperative testing shows a hemoglobin of 8.6 g/dL from previously unrecognized iron deficiency, a platelet count of 92,000/mm³, and a bicarbonate of 18 mEq/L.{FIG}Which of the following is the most appropriate next step?",
